{"connection_id": "BC-4bc8c834e2f93db9424c", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.7.29", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The remaining time is shortened", "note": "The commentary says a long life is seen as compressed when its end approaches; Paul tells believers the appointed time has grown short and therefore their ordinary life relations must be held lightly."}
{"connection_id": "BC-96c4a90295c8755820e6", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.7.31", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The present form of the world is passing", "note": "The commentary says a seemingly stable span is already vanishing; Paul tells those engaged with the world not to live as though its present form were lasting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0df452b2a76354e124e3", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.2.13", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Fathers and young people addressed separately", "note": "The commentary names distinct stages of a life; the letter addresses fathers and young people with different spiritual descriptions, an analogy through communal age categories rather than a literal lifespan sequence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cf871b698b6a7b013794", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.24", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Human flesh as grass", "note": "The commentary reduces a human lifetime to a passing interval; Peter applies Isaiah's fading-grass image to all flesh, making mortal brevity part of his appeal to a community born through the gospel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bd2b4e436ce8d99fcab8", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.25", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Enduring word against passing life", "note": "The commentary joins short human life to truth that can hold people together; Peter completes the Isaiah citation by contrasting fading humanity with the Lord's enduring word and identifies that word with what was proclaimed to his hearers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17b8736b59e8dc73b837", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.1.3", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "work of faith; labor of love; endurance of hope", "note": "The commentary names faith, good works, and patience as the actions of those who escape loss; Paul recalls this community's work, labor, and endurance in faith, love, and hope, preserving the same linked ethical pattern."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b18c3eaa2e48d8df162a", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.3.10", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Night-and-day prayer seeks to strengthen others", "note": "The commentary makes mutual support stretch through both parts of the day; Paul describes earnest night-and-day prayer to see his hearers again and supply what their faith lacks."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2899313ea7e4e11b7e66", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.1", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Times and seasons introduce the final Day", "note": "The commentary moves from named periods to a sudden terminal hour; Paul explicitly invokes times and seasons before describing the Lord's Day as unexpectedly arriving in the following verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1b817a6f0724ef785bb1", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.11", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Encourage and build one another", "note": "The commentary's repeated reciprocal counsel makes a durable community; Paul explicitly tells believers to encourage one another and build one another up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a1c6989e74f82bb09aad", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "admonish, encourage, support; be patient with all", "note": "The commentary distinguishes counsel in truth from counsel in patience; Paul assigns different kinds of mutual care and closes with patience toward all, a close ethical configuration of the paired exhortations."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d4e0e4ef04f3e70bc240", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Admonish, help, and be patient with all", "note": "The commentary couples mutual counsel with patience; this instruction names admonishing the idle, helping the weak, and being patient with everyone as communal practices."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4e2e97e94a122f419a52", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.2", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Day of the Lord arrives during night", "note": "The commentary juxtaposes the day-night pair with the sudden end of a seeming long stay; Paul says the Lord's day comes like a thief in the night, challenging complacency about the remaining time."}

{"connection_id": "BC-8b06dc60ce83670bc4db", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.5", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Believers belong to day, not night", "note": "The commentary makes remaining people a distinct group amid the alternation of night and day; Paul calls believers children of light and day, assigning the temporal images an ethical identity."}
{"connection_id": "BC-91645bb0758446c1e213", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.6", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Wakefulness instead of sleep", "note": "The commentary develops short sleep and patient alertness across time; Paul tells the community not to sleep as others do but to keep awake and sober in view of the approaching day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1585b21158e09be00f72", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.6.18", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Rich are to become rich in good works", "note": "The commentary contrasts accumulating possessions with righteous action that endures; Paul instructs the rich to be rich in good works and generous to others."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d6329f10073f6fa4ac18", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.6.19", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Store a foundation for the future life", "note": "The commentary's accumulation motif ends at the grave unless joined to right deeds; Paul pictures generosity as storing a firm foundation for the future so that people may grasp true life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5f8d8215bcad08c1923f", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.16", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Outer decline, daily inner renewal", "note": "The commentary tracks bodily life through aging while patience persists across days; Paul says the outer person wastes away but the inner person is renewed day by day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0146839a4cef86918b4b", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.6.2", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Now is the accepted time and day of rescue", "note": "The commentary's finite interval calls for righteous response before the end; Paul applies a promise about the favorable time and salvation day to his hearers' present now."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ebc50f40812c93cee934", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.15", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Divine patience counted as salvation", "note": "The commentary joins the waiting interval to the chance to remain among the saved; Peter explicitly asks readers to regard the Lord's patience as salvation, supplying the purpose of the delay."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4f99809fe73c9057ac49", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.8", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "one day like a thousand years; a thousand years like one day", "note": "The commentary says the entire lifespan becomes an evening or a day-hour; Peter cites the Lord's different scale of time, explicitly comparing a day with a millennium."}
{"connection_id": "BC-84ca31da01a2064cf94b", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.8", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "One day and a thousand years", "note": "The commentary contrasts long duration with its apparent contraction; this verse reversibly compares one day and a thousand years before the Lord, relativizing ordinary measures of waiting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0284d5309ebff16612ef", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.9", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Delayed promise and divine patience", "note": "The commentary connects patience to the true promise through a shrinking lifetime; this verse says the promised coming is not slow as some reckon but delayed in divine patience to allow repentance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5b124a1a65ecb04040af", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.3.8", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Night-and-day labor spares the community", "note": "The commentary connects righteous work across the daily cycle with people sustaining one another; Paul says his group worked night and day so they would burden none of the believers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-911f12eb0ab6099f1a22", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.2", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Exhort at every season with patience", "note": "The commentary's counsel and patience fill successive times; the charge to proclaim the word in season and out of season includes correction and exhortation with complete patience and teaching."}

{"connection_id": "BC-1d92f6c4f4cf16e3a7a6", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.4.21", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Companionship sought before winter", "note": "The commentary links winter's coming with people maintaining one another through time; Paul urges his addressee to come before winter, making the seasonal deadline matter for their meeting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-374960493af923be2409", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.17.26", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Appointed periods for human peoples", "note": "The commentary divides time into assigned intervals while people remain joined; Paul says God made every nation from one and determined their appointed times and dwelling boundaries."}
{"connection_id": "BC-79381ab77d3e606b56be", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.20.31", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Three years of night-and-day admonition", "note": "The commentary ties mutual counsel to morning/evening and a lasting interval; Paul recalls three years in which he warned each person night and day with tears."}
{"connection_id": "BC-71d2ef3956c6fbdd9be4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.16", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teach and admonish one another", "note": "The commentary's tawasaw makes counsel reciprocal; Paul describes a community teaching and admonishing one another through wisdom and song, a communal practice parallel to that reciprocal relation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-31a84b9665050ae81299", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.16", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Teach and admonish one another", "note": "The commentary defines the surviving group through mutual counsel; Colossians asks believers to let Christ's word dwell among them as they teach and admonish one another wisely."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8be6ecf54d844668ab63", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Speaking truth together builds maturity", "note": "The commentary makes counsel in truth a way people are joined; speaking truth in love is the means by which members grow toward their common head, Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-022c41e4ce07abddb4d4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.16", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The body joined by every working part", "note": "The commentary says the people who remain are added to one another; the body is joined and held together as each part works, building itself up in love."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a0fa4c81c2e98c5c146", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to neighbor; members of one another", "note": "The commentary pairs mutual counsel with haqq; Paul commands truthful speech to a neighbor because the speakers are members of one another, making truth-telling the practice that sustains their shared body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3c0431765469d33ff7c5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Speak truth as members of one another", "note": "The commentary brings truth and people being joined into one image; Ephesians gives membership in one body as the reason for each person to speak truth to a neighbor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-268deff93d7ebf1583aa", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.5.16", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "make the most of the time", "note": "The commentary says number-chasing consumes time unnoticed and that good action matters within a short life; Paul tells readers to make the most of the time because the days are evil, turning the finite span into an ethical opportunity."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e34ce694a5956289a07f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.5.16", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Use the time because days are evil", "note": "The commentary makes limited time the setting for righteous action; Ephesians asks its hearers to make the most of the time because the days are evil."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fa9651401ceb3d013028", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.10", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Present opportunity used for good to all", "note": "The commentary says righteous deeds and mutual support occupy limited time; Paul says that while opportunity remains believers should do good to everyone, especially fellow believers."}

{"connection_id": "BC-67c304a4a8f589c847c6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing good; harvest at the proper time; do not give up", "note": "The commentary joins righteous deeds to mutual exhortation and patience; Paul says not to tire of doing good because harvest comes at the proper time if one does not give up, joining all three actions in one claim."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ed737dab71bb2428b482", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.9", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Good action sustained until its season", "note": "The commentary joins righteous deeds and patience across time; Paul says not to grow weary in doing good because a harvest will come at its proper time if people do not give up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-56cd2fc6163e47ee0c03", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "consider one another; provoke love and good works", "note": "The commentary says people join through reciprocal exhortation and righteous action; Hebrews makes the relation active by telling readers to consider one another and stir up love and good works."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9395a403fb1f3cc4c79b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Stir one another to good works", "note": "The commentary makes shared righteous action part of how people remain connected; Hebrews asks believers to consider one another so as to provoke love and good deeds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4cace0c203a493790432", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage one another as the Day approaches", "note": "The commentary joins human exhortation to long time and the final gathering; Hebrews commands mutual encouragement as the Day draws near, making the approaching end a reason to remain connected."}
{"connection_id": "BC-02c74d9dafae2e9a53f8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Gather and encourage as the Day approaches", "note": "The commentary connects communal exhortation to passing time; Hebrews opposes abandoning assembly and urges increasingly mutual encouragement as the approaching Day is seen."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8f9ab119b5e1ecb8f288", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance after doing God's will; receive the promise", "note": "The commentary couples patience with right action; Hebrews says endurance is needed after doing God's will in order to receive what was promised, making persistence the bridge between action and outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ce259d6579535863cf1e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.36", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Endurance receives the promised thing", "note": "The commentary joins patience to the true promise; Hebrews says endurance is needed after doing God's will so that hearers may receive what was promised."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c0966331d10406966e74", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.11", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "present pain; later fruit of righteousness", "note": "The commentary links sabr with cold and waiting and gives righteous action as the survivor's practice; Hebrews says discipline later yields peaceful fruit of righteousness to those trained by it, explicitly making endurance fruitful over time."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7c574cf5d2bcb8e5d10e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "daily exhortation of one another", "note": "The commentary's tawasaw is reciprocal counsel within a chain; Hebrews says to exhort one another every day so none is hardened, adding a daily rhythm and a reason for the practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-59dac5f7b6b9b9f8ee74", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Exhort one another every day", "note": "The commentary's people remain joined through reciprocal counsel across linked days; Hebrews commands daily mutual exhortation while it is called Today, to prevent hardening through sin."}
{"connection_id": "BC-71beb6a8dad7c65c3971", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.4.7", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "A new Today after a long time", "note": "The commentary describes time as linked parts in which an appeal remains open; Hebrews says God appoints another day called Today after a long time, using David's warning to demand a present response."}

